> **Read the two right-hand columns.** From FY2016 to FY2021 the annual bonus paid out at **100% of maximum in six consecutive years**, and the LTIP at 100% in three. That is not a performance-linked outcome; it is a formula that could not fail, because the bonus was funded as a direct share of Adjusted Profit Before Tax and profit tracked markets. From FY2022 the same two columns fall to 74/99, 25/58, 20/37, 13/6 and finally **0/0**. The remuneration framework and the shareholder experience are now, at last, moving together.

