**Three details worth noting.** First, the LTIP line is instructive. In FY2024 a base value of £324k was cut to £179k by a **£145k share price depreciation adjustment**; in FY2025 a £54k base was cut to £30k by a £24k adjustment. **The plan claws back for a falling share price on the way out, as well as failing to vest on the way in.** Second, the cash component has gone to zero: the cash bonus was 45% and 35% of salary in FY2024, 0% in FY2025 (100% deferral), and there was no bonus at all in FY2026. Third, FY2026 total remuneration for both executives combined was **£1,178k**, against a policy maximum for the two of roughly **£8.4m**. They were paid approximately **14% of what the policy permits.** For scale, the executives' combined annual bonus represented just **1.8% of the group-wide bonus pool** in FY2025 (FY2024: 2.1%) — 1.1% to the CEO and 0.7% to the CFO.

